<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\|S_{i}-S_{j}\|_{F}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+SVX+B\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\|S_{i}-S_{j}\|_{F}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+SVX+B\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">where (i) from Lemma 1; (ii) rearranging; (iii) uses triangle inequality and applies the assumptions on the bounds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging Equation <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> into Equation <a href="#A1.Ex25" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})-\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})-\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\|\chi_{i}-\chi_{j}\|_{F}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\|\chi_{i}-\chi_{j}\|_{F}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})=\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})=\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}K}{D^{3/2}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}K}{D^{3/2}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]</annotation></semantics></math> be an affine function of <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound the gradient difference w.r.t <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})-\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})\|_{F}\leq f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})-\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})\|_{F}\leq f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bound for <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.SS1.p15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Similarly, we have the following bound for the third term</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{W_{K}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})-\nabla_{W_{K}}\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})\|_{F}\leq f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{W_{K}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})-\nabla_{W_{K}}\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi_{\text{target}}^{t})\|_{F}\leq f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})=\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}Q}{{D^{3/2}}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}Q}{{D^{3/2}}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})=\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}Q}{{D^{3/2}}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}Q}{{D^{3/2}}}\Big[4\alpha+2SVX+B\Big]</annotation></semantics></math> be affine function of <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging all these expressions in <a href="#A1.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ A.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, we have the following expression for the upper bound of the target-model gradient difference</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{f_{1}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{f_{1}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Cauchy-Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{f_{1}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sqrt{f_{1}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}+f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq|f_{1}(\epsilon^{\prime})|+|f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})|+|f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq|f_{1}(\epsilon^{\prime})|+|f_{2}(\epsilon^{\prime})|+|f_{3}(\epsilon^{\prime})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\Bigg[\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}(K+Q)}{D^{3/2}}+\bigg(\frac{8SX^{2}V}{N}+\frac{4BX}{N}\bigg)\Bigg]}_{c_{1}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\Bigg[\frac{2\sqrt{N}V^{2}X^{4}(K+Q)}{D^{3/2}}+\bigg(\frac{8SX^{2}V}{N}+\frac{4BX}{N}\bigg)\Bigg]}_{c_{1}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}}{{D^{3/2}}}\Big[(4\alpha+2SVX+B)(Q+K)\Big]+\frac{4SX}{N}(4SXV+3B)}_{c_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\frac{2\sqrt{N}VX^{3}}{{D^{3/2}}}\Big[(4\alpha+2SVX+B)(Q+K)\Big]+\frac{4SX}{N}(4SXV+3B)}_{c_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume the model weights <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded by <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{c}{\sqrt{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>c</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{c}{\sqrt{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi^{t}_{\text{target}}\|\leq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi^{t}_{\text{target}}\|\leq c</annotation></semantics></math>.
We further assume the ground-truth embedding <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and loss <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded.
Such boundedness assumptions are standard in theoretical analyses of Transformers, including generalization and stability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>, as well as gradient-based optimization dynamics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
In practice, they are enforced by weight decay, and layer/activation normalization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2020</a>)</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> passes through an RMS normalization layer with gain <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\leq g\sqrt{ND}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\leq g\sqrt{ND}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under this setting, the constants <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> simplify to:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}\!\left(\tfrac{4}{\sqrt{3}}N^{2}\sqrt{ND}\,c^{3}g^{4}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.654em;" width="0.654em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}\!\left(\tfrac{4}{\sqrt{3}}N^{2}\sqrt{ND}\,c^{3}g^{4}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}\!\left(\tfrac{8}{3\sqrt{3}}N^{3}\sqrt{D}\,c^{2}g^{4}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.654em;" width="0.654em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{O}\!\left(\tfrac{8}{3\sqrt{3}}N^{3}\sqrt{D}\,c^{2}g^{4}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">If the RMS gain is sufficiently small, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g&lt;N^{-\nicefrac{{5}}{{8}}}D^{-\nicefrac{{1}}{{8}}}c^{-\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad g^{4}&lt;N^{-\nicefrac{{5}}{{2}}}D^{-\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}c^{-3}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">5</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">8</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">8</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">5</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g&lt;N^{-\nicefrac{{5}}{{8}}}D^{-\nicefrac{{1}}{{8}}}c^{-\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad g^{4}&lt;N^{-\nicefrac{{5}}{{2}}}D^{-\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}c^{-3},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p23.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p23.2.1" class="ltx_text">then the bounds on <math id="A1.SS1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> reduce to:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\tfrac{4}{\sqrt{3}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\tfrac{4}{\sqrt{3}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\tfrac{8\sqrt{N}}{3\sqrt{3}c}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\tfrac{8\sqrt{N}}{3\sqrt{3}c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the gradient distance can be bounded as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq\tfrac{4}{\sqrt{3}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\tfrac{8\sqrt{N}}{3\sqrt{3}c}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq\tfrac{4}{\sqrt{3}}\cdot\epsilon^{\prime}+\tfrac{8\sqrt{N}}{3\sqrt{3}c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1.2 Bounding Gradient Distance Throughout Finetuning ‣ 4.1 Finding Clusters of Examples with Similar Gradient ‣ 4 Method: Extracting Non-redundant Subsets of the VIT Data ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first have the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang, 2023</a>)</cite>, Theorem 1.8)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let f: <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a twice continuously differentiable function. Given <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, for every <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=x+t(y-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=x+t(y-x)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant, <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta=\sup\|\nabla^{2}f(x)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta=\sup\|\nabla^{2}f(x)\|</annotation></semantics></math> , such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla f(z)-\nabla f(x)\|_{F}\leq\zeta\|z-x\|_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla f(z)-\nabla f(x)\|_{F}\leq\zeta\|z-x\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{\leq}}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}+\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}+\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(i)}}{{\leq}}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}+\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}+\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(ii)}}{{\leq}}2\beta\|\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}}-\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}}\|+\Delta^{t_{1}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(ii)}}{{\leq}}2\beta\|\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}}-\phi^{t_{1}}_{\text{target}}\|+\Delta^{t_{1}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(iii)}}{{\leq}}2\delta\beta+\Delta^{t_{1}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(iii)}}{{\leq}}2\delta\beta+\Delta^{t_{1}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">where (i) from triangle inequality; (ii) from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (( , ), Theorem 1.8). ‣ A.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>; (iii) from bounded curvature assumption and the definition of <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq 2\delta\beta+\Delta^{t_{2}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq 2\delta\beta+\Delta^{t_{2}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these two above inequalities, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq 2\delta\beta+\max\{\Delta^{t_{1}}_{ij},\Delta^{t_{2}}_{ij}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>target</mtext><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})-\nabla\mathcal{L}_{j}(\phi^{t_{z}}_{\text{target}})\|_{F}\leq 2\delta\beta+\max\{\Delta^{t_{1}}_{ij},\Delta^{t_{2}}_{ij}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Convergence of XMAS</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convergence of XMAS)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumptions of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.1.2 Bounding Gradient Distance Throughout Finetuning ‣ 4.1 Finding Clusters of Examples with Similar Gradient ‣ 4 Method: Extracting Non-redundant Subsets of the VIT Data ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, applying incremental gradient methods with stepsize <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> on subsets found by XMAS, converges to a neighborhood of the solution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> found by training on full data:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\phi^{t+1}-\phi^{*}\|^{2}\leq(1-\eta c^{\prime})^{t+1}\|\phi^{t}-\phi^{*}\|^{2}+\frac{2\xi R^{\prime}}{c^{\prime 2}}+\eta B^{2}\left(\frac{r_{\min}}{k}\right)^{2}g_{\max}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\phi^{t+1}-\phi^{*}\|^{2}\leq(1-\eta c^{\prime})^{t+1}\|\phi^{t}-\phi^{*}\|^{2}+\frac{2\xi R^{\prime}}{c^{\prime 2}}+\eta B^{2}\left(\frac{r_{\min}}{k}\right)^{2}g_{\max}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\leq\|H\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\leq\|H\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is the total size of the subset, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest gradient norm of individual examples during training, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\min},r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\min},r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, are the size of the smallest and largest clusters, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}=\min\{d_{0},Bg_{\max}+\xi/c^{\prime}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}=\min\{d_{0},Bg_{\max}+\xi/c^{\prime}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=\|\phi^{0}-\phi^{*}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=\|\phi^{0}-\phi^{*}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial distance to the optimal solution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=K[r_{\min}\Delta_{2}+(r_{\max}-r_{\min})g_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=K[r_{\min}\Delta_{2}+(r_{\max}-r_{\min})g_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our proof is similar to the one in S2L <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>, Appendix A.2)</cite>. We provide the details in order to ensure completeness.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, assume we select <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> examples from each cluster and we have <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq\min_{j\in[K]}|C_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq\min_{j\in[K]}|C_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the error of the subset in capturing the full gradient will be</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\leq\sum_{j}(|C_{j}|-k)\left(\bar{g}_{j}+\Delta\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\leq\sum_{j}(|C_{j}|-k)\left(\bar{g}_{j}+\Delta\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the norm of the average gradient of all samples from <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum error in gradients between two different samples.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">In practice, we can weight elements of the subset by <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\min}/k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\min}/k</annotation></semantics></math>, which has a similar effect to scaling the step size when training on the subset. Let <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\max}=\max_{j}\|g_{j}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\max}=\max_{j}\|g_{j}\|</annotation></semantics></math> be the maximum gradient norm during training, <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}=\max_{j}|C_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}=\max_{j}|C_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\min}=\min_{j}|C_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\min}=\min_{j}|C_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we get</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{\prime}\leq\sum_{j}\left[(r_{\min}-k)\Delta+(|C_{j}|-r_{\min})(\bar{g}_{j}+\Delta)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{\prime}\leq\sum_{j}\left[(r_{\min}-k)\Delta+(|C_{j}|-r_{\min})(\bar{g}_{j}+\Delta)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq K\left[r_{\min}\Delta+(r_{\max}-r_{\min})g_{\max}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq K\left[r_{\min}\Delta+(r_{\max}-r_{\min})g_{\max}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first term in the RHS of Eq. (7) is the error of the subset selected from <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to capture its full gradient and the second term is due to selecting the same number of examples, <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, from the larger clusters. Using the above error and following the proof of Theorem 1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mirzasoleiman et al. (2020)</a></cite>, for a constant step size <math id="A1.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq 1/c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq 1/c</annotation></semantics></math> we get:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta^{t+1}-\theta^{*}\|^{2}\leq(1-\alpha c)^{t+1}\|\theta^{t}-\theta^{*}\|^{2}+\frac{2\xi^{\prime}R}{c^{2}}+\alpha B^{2}\left(\frac{r_{\min}}{k}\right)^{2}g_{\max}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta^{t+1}-\theta^{*}\|^{2}\leq(1-\alpha c)^{t+1}\|\theta^{t}-\theta^{*}\|^{2}+\frac{2\xi^{\prime}R}{c^{2}}+\alpha B^{2}\left(\frac{r_{\min}}{k}\right)^{2}g_{\max}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leq\|H\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leq\|H\|</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=k\cdot K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=k\cdot K</annotation></semantics></math> is the total size of the subset, <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\min\{d_{0},Bg_{\max}+\xi^{\prime}/c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\min\{d_{0},Bg_{\max}+\xi^{\prime}/c\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=\|\theta^{0}-\theta^{*}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=\|\theta^{0}-\theta^{*}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial distance to the optimal solution <math id="A1.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq|C_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq|C_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math> for any cluster <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can simply add <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{\min}/k-1)\cdot\hat{g}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{\min}/k-1)\cdot\hat{g}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for the corresponding clusters, where <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the norm of the total gradient of cluster <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and we replace <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (7) with the size of smallest cluster that has larger than <math id="A1.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> examples.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proofs of Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying chain rule and simplifying, we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{W_{V}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})=\nabla_{F_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{W_{V}}F_{i}(\phi^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{W_{V}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})=\nabla_{F_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{W_{V}}F_{i}(\phi^{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=(F_{i}-Y_{i})(S_{i}X_{i}\otimes I_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=(F_{i}-Y_{i})(S_{i}X_{i}\otimes I_{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying chain rule and simplifying, we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})=\nabla_{F_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{S_{i}}F_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{W_{Q}}A_{i}(\phi^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})=\nabla_{F_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{S_{i}}F_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot\nabla_{W_{Q}}A_{i}(\phi^{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=(F_{i}-Y_{i})(I_{N}\otimes W_{V}^{T}X_{i}^{T})\cdot\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot(\frac{X_{i}\otimes X_{i}W_{K}}{\sqrt{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=(F_{i}-Y_{i})(I_{N}\otimes W_{V}^{T}X_{i}^{T})\cdot\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i}(\phi^{t})\cdot(\frac{X_{i}\otimes X_{i}W_{K}}{\sqrt{D}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proceeding as above for <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{Q}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{W_{K}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})=(S_{i}X_{i}W_{V}-y_{i})(I_{N}\otimes W_{V}^{T}X_{i}^{T})\frac{\partial S_{i}}{\partial A_{i}}\bigg(\frac{X_{i}\otimes X_{i}W_{Q}}{\sqrt{D}}\bigg)\Lambda_{d,D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{W_{K}}\mathcal{L}_{i}(\phi^{t})=(S_{i}X_{i}W_{V}-y_{i})(I_{N}\otimes W_{V}^{T}X_{i}^{T})\frac{\partial S_{i}}{\partial A_{i}}\bigg(\frac{X_{i}\otimes X_{i}W_{Q}}{\sqrt{D}}\bigg)\Lambda_{d,D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{d,D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{d,D}</annotation></semantics></math> is the commutation matrix.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a single sample, <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=softmax(A_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=softmax(A_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where softmax is applied row-wise to A. The expression for a single element in <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> present at (j, k) is given as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{i})_{jk}=\frac{e^{(A_{i})_{jk}}}{\sum_{z=1}^{L}e^{(A_{i})_{jz}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{i})_{jk}=\frac{e^{(A_{i})_{jk}}}{\sum_{z=1}^{L}e^{(A_{i})_{jz}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now, clearly, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{mn}}=0\;\;\text{if}\;j\neq m" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.560em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{mn}}=0\;\;\text{if}\;j\neq m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now for a specific row, <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the Jacobian of the <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> wrt the <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is given as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J^{(j)}_{kn}=\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{jn}}=\begin{cases}(S_{i})_{jk}\Big(1-(S_{i})_{jk}\Big)&amp;\text{if}\;k=n\\
-(S_{i})_{jk}(S_{i})_{jn}&amp;\text{if}\;k\neq n\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J^{(j)}_{kn}=\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{jn}}=\begin{cases}(S_{i})_{jk}\Big(1-(S_{i})_{jk}\Big)&amp;\text{if}\;k=n\\
-(S_{i})_{jk}(S_{i})_{jn}&amp;\text{if}\;k\neq n\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(S_{i})_{jk}\Big(\delta_{kn}-(S_{i})_{kn}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(S_{i})_{jk}\Big(\delta_{kn}-(S_{i})_{kn}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{jm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{jm}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Kronecker delta (1 if j=m, 0 otherwise).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now the complete Jacobian of the attention matrix can be written as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}=\delta_{jm}(S_{i})_{jk}\Big(\delta_{kn}-(S_{i})_{kn}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}=\delta_{jm}(S_{i})_{jk}\Big(\delta_{kn}-(S_{i})_{kn}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{jm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{jm}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{kn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{kn}</annotation></semantics></math> are the Kronecker deltas.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following is the expression for the Frobenius Norm of this Jacobian:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sum_{m=1}^{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\bigg(\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{mn}}\bigg)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sum_{m=1}^{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\bigg(\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{mn}}\bigg)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sum_{m=1}^{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\bigg(\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{jn}}\bigg)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\sum_{m=1}^{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\bigg(\frac{\partial(S_{i})_{jk}}{\partial(A_{i})_{jn}}\bigg)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now computing <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> for a single row <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, let <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{p}^{(j)}=\sum_{q=1}^{N}(S_{i})_{jq}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{p}^{(j)}=\sum_{q=1}^{N}(S_{i})_{jq}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> Then we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Big(J^{(j)}_{kn}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Big(J^{(j)}_{kn}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{N}\Big((S_{i})_{jk}(1-(S_{i})_{jk})\Big)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sum_{n\neq k}\Big(-(S_{i})_{jk}(S_{i})_{jn}\Big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{N}\Big((S_{i})_{jk}(1-(S_{i})_{jk})\Big)^{2}+\sum_{k=1}^{N}\sum_{n\neq k}\Big(-(S_{i})_{jk}(S_{i})_{jn}\Big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\xi_{2}^{(j)}-2\xi_{3}^{(j)}+\Big(\xi_{2}^{(j)}\Big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\xi_{2}^{(j)}-2\xi_{3}^{(j)}+\Big(\xi_{2}^{(j)}\Big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now the maximum value of <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under constraints, <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{1}^{(j)}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{1}^{(j)}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{i})_{jq}\geq 0\;\;\forall q\in\{0,1,2,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.727em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{i})_{jq}\geq 0\;\;\forall q\in\{0,1,2,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>, is <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math> and is achieved when exactly two <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{i})_{jq}=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{i})_{jq}=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging this in equation  <a href="#A1.Ex47" title="In Proof. ‣ A.4 Proofs of Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>, we get</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\sum_{j=1}^{N}\Big(\frac{1}{4}\Big)=\frac{N}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\|J^{(j)}\|_{F}^{2}\leq\sum_{j=1}^{N}\Big(\frac{1}{4}\Big)=\frac{N}{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}\leq\frac{\sqrt{N}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|(\nabla_{A_{i}}S_{i})_{jkmn}\|_{F}\leq\frac{\sqrt{N}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional experimental settings</h2>

<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="A2.F5.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:352.5pt;height:195.6pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-75.5pt,41.9pt) scale(0.7,0.7) ;"><img src="2510.01454v1/xmas_figure.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/386;" width="685" height="386" alt="Refer to caption">
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>XMAS employs a small proxy VLM to find alignment trajectory for examples in the fine-tuning data. Examples with similar alignment trajectory have similar gradients during instruction tuning. Then, it clusters the alignment trajectories and sample a balanced subset of examples with more stable trajectories from the clusters.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models.</span> For the target LVLMs, we use the pre-trained LLaVA-1.5-7B and LLaVA-1.5-13B models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024a)</a></cite>.
For the proxy models, we use the TinyLLaVA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2024</a>)</cite> with 2 different scales 0.5B and 2.0B. The default one is TinyLLaVA 2.0B due to its superior performance. Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix B Additional experimental settings ‣ Data Selection for Fine-tuning Vision Language Models via Cross Modal Alignment Trajectories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes the language model and vision encoder of different models used in our experiment.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Details of the model architectures used in our experiments are provided below. Model names correspond to their repository names on HuggingFace.</figcaption>
